let __v_455 = pyrt::literals::decode("[{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"spinach\",\"baby spinach\",\"bag of spinach\",\"spinach leaves\"]},\"A bag of spinach keeps about 5 days in the salad drawer and a whole unopened bag a week longer, and the date on the bag is the day to finish it by rather than a day it is still good after. Pick out anything slimy before it spreads, don't wash the leaves until you use them, and a bag that has only gone limp is fine wilted into a curry or an omelette.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"rice\",\"white rice\",\"basmati rice\",\"long grain rice\",\"brown rice\"]},\"Dry rice keeps for years in a sealed jar in a cupboard, and the date on the bag is a best-before rather than a use-by. Cooked rice is the one to be strict about: cool it within an hour, box it, and keep it no more than 24 hours in the fridge - reheating does not kill the spores that grow in rice left warm.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"guacamole\",\"taramasalata\",\"tarama\",\"tzatziki\",\"soured cream dip\",\"onion dip\"]},\"Once opened, a tub of tzatziki or taramasalata keeps about 3 days in the fridge and guacamole a day or two, because avocado browns and sours fastest: the date on the lid is for the sealed pot, so judge it by look and smell after that. Press cling film down onto guacamole to keep the air off it, keep all of them cold, and bin anything that smells sour, fizzes or has mould.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"next day\",\"the next day\"]}]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"hummus\",\"houmous\",\"humous\"]},\"Hummus keeps about a week in the fridge in a sealed tub, and 3 to 4 days once a spoon has been in it: the date on the lid is for the sealed pot, so a couple of days past it is usually fine. A film of water on top is normal, so stir it in. Bin it if it smells sour or fizzy, or if there is mould.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"next day\",\"the next day\"]}]}]")?;
