let __v_1496 = Value::from("Still fine to eat: soft is damp, not spoilage, and heat takes the damp back out. Bin them instead if there is mould on any of them, or if they smell of old paint or crayons, which is the oil in them going rancid.");
frame.store("_CRUNCH_VERDICT", __v_1496.clone())?;
let __v_1497 = Value::from("Soft, not spoilt: they have taken damp out of the air. Spread them on a tray and give them 4 to 5 minutes at 150C, then leave them to cool - they crisp as they cool, not in the oven. Popped corn and nuts take the same and 3 minutes is enough; a biscuit that has gone chewy comes back the same way.");
frame.store("_CRUNCH_FIX", __v_1497.clone())?;
let __v_1498 = Value::from("To keep the crunch, tip them into a jar or a tin with a tight lid rather than leaving them in the bag, which breathes, and keep them in a cupboard rather than the fridge, which is damp. A piece of kitchen paper in the box takes up the damp the same way.");
frame.store("_CRUNCH_KEEP", __v_1498.clone())?;
let __v_1499 = Value::from("That clear liquid is whey, and it belongs to the yogurt: stir it back in. Yogurt that has separated into curds and watery liquid and smells sharp, fizzy or of alcohol is the one to bin.");
frame.store("_YOGHURT_WHEY", __v_1499.clone())?;
let __v_1500 = Value::from("Yogurt separates as the whey rises, and spooning from the same spot makes it happen sooner: take from the side and stir the tub before you serve it. Plain yogurt keeps about a week past the date once it is open, and stirring is all a watery tub needs; a sharp or fizzy smell is when to bin it.");
frame.store("_YOGHURT_FIX", __v_1500.clone())?;
let __v_1501 = Value::from("Clumped salt has taken damp, not gone off: break it up with the back of a spoon and it still tastes of salt and works the same in cooking. A few grains of rice or a piece of dry cracker in the jar keeps it running, and a lidded jar in a dry cupboard keeps it clump-free where the paper packet does not.");
frame.store("_SALT_CLUMPS", __v_1501.clone())?;
let __v_1502 = Value::from("Lumps in flour are damp, not spoilage: sift it and it is fine to bake with. If it also smells musty or sour, or the lumps are moving, bin the bag - that is mites - wipe the shelf out and keep the next bag in a sealed jar.");
frame.store("_FLOUR_LUMPS", __v_1502.clone())?;
